1. **Perimeter of the large equilateral triangle:**
   The perimeter of the large equilateral triangle is given as \(60 \text{ cm}\). Since an equilateral triangle has three equal sides, each side of the large triangle is:
   \[
   \frac{60}{3} = 20 \text{ cm}
   \]

2. **Perimeter of the irregular hexagon:**
   The perimeter of the irregular hexagon is given as \(40 \text{ cm}\). The hexagon is formed by cutting off three smaller equilateral triangles from the corners of the large triangle. Each side of the hexagon is a side of one of these smaller triangles.

