   - An Eulerian path exists in a graph if exactly 0 or 2 vertices have an odd degree.
   - Calculate the degree of each vertex:
     - \( S \): degree 2 (connected to \( P \) and \( R \))
     - \( P \): degree 2 (connected to \( S \) and \( Q \))
