     - \( R \): degree 2 (connected to \( Q \) and \( S \))
   - Only \( Q \) has an odd degree (3), and \( S \) has an even degree (2). This satisfies the condition for an Eulerian path starting at \( S \) and ending at \( Q \).

3. **Find Possible Routes:**
