   \[
   \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} s \leq \frac{10\sqrt{3}}{\sqrt{37}}
   \]
   Solving for \(s\):
   \[
   s \leq \frac{20}{\sqrt{37}}
   \]

6. **Area Calculation:**
   Using the maximum possible side length \(s = \frac{20}{\sqrt{37}}\), the area of the equilateral triangle is:
