   The slope of the tangent line at \( P \) is \( -\frac{\frac{2}{5} - 1}{\frac{4}{5}} = -\frac{-\frac{3}{5}}{\frac{4}{5}} = \frac{3}{4} \). The equation of the tangent line in point-slope form is:
