   - \( BC + CD > BD \) → \( 17 + 5 > BD \) → \( 22 > BD \)
   - \( BC + BD > CD \) → \( 17 + BD > 5 \) → \( BD > -12 \) (This is always true since \( BD \) is positive)
   - \( CD + BD > BC \) → \( 5 + BD > 17 \) → \( BD > 12 \)

   From these inequalities, \( BD > 12 \).

### Combining the Inequalities:
From the inequalities derived from both triangles:
- \( 4 < BD < 14 \) (from \( ABD \))
- \( BD > 12 \) (from \( BCD \))

The only integer value that satisfies both conditions is \( BD = 13 \).

Answer: \boxed{13}
