   - Each vertex is equally spaced on the circumference of the unit circle.
   - The length of a chord (edge or diagonal) in a unit circle can be calculated using the formula \( 2 \sin\left(\frac{k\pi}{n}\right) \), where \( k \) is the number of steps between vertices, and \( n \) is the number of sides (7 in this case).

