   - The area of square \(EFGH\) is \(s^2\).
   - The area of rectangle \(ABCD\) is \(lw\).

3. **Given Information:**
   - Rectangle \(ABCD\) shares \(50\%\) of its area with square \(EFGH\). This means the overlapping area is \(0.5 \times lw\).
   - Square \(EFGH\) shares \(20\%\) of its area with rectangle \(ABCD\). This means the overlapping area is \(0.2 \times s^2\).

