   The total area of the figure is the sum of the areas of the outer equilateral triangle and the inner equilateral triangle.
   \[
   \text{Total Area} = \text{Area of Outer Triangle} + \text{Area of Inner Triangle} = 16 + 1 = 17
   \]

2. **Area of the Three Trapezoids:**
   The three trapezoids are congruent, so their combined area is the total area of the figure minus the area of the inner triangle.
