### Step 1: Identify the Geometry
The belt forms a triangle around the three circles. Each side of the triangle is tangent to two circles, and the points of tangency are at the points where the circles touch each other.

### Step 2: Calculate the Distance Between Centers of Two Adjacent Circles
The distance between the centers of two adjacent circles is the sum of their radii:
\[
d = 10 + 10 = 20 \text{ cm}
\]

