The straight segments of the belt are the sides of an equilateral triangle with side length equal to the distance between the centers of two adjacent circles:
\[
\text{Length of each straight segment} = 20 \text{ cm}
\]
Since there are three such segments:
\[
\text{Total length of straight segments} = 3 \times 20 = 60 \text{ cm}
\]

