\[
\text{Total Surface Area} = \text{Curved Surface Area} + \text{Area of Two Rectangular Faces} + \text{Area of Semicircular Base}
\]
\[
\text{Total Surface Area} = 60\pi + 120 + 18\pi = 78\pi + 120 \text{ cm}^2
\]

Thus, the total surface area of the solid is \(78\pi + 120\) square centimeters.

