   - The area of \( R \) is \( T \times \left(\frac{a}{\sqrt{2}}\right)^2 = T \times \frac{a^2}{2} \).
   - The proportion of the area of \( S \) contained within \( R \) is:
     \[
     \frac{\text{Area of } R}{\text{Area of } S} = \frac{T \times \frac{a^2}{2}}{a^2} = \frac{T}{2}
