From the image, we know the base of the triangle is 10 units. We need to find the height. The height can be found using the Pythagorean theorem in one of the right triangles formed by the height, half of the base, and one of the equal sides.

The length of the equal side is 13 units, and half of the base is \( \frac{10}{2} = 5 \) units. Let \( h \) be the height. According to the Pythagorean theorem:

