   - A torus is formed by rotating a circle (the small circle) around an axis that lies in the same plane as the circle but does not intersect it.
   - The distance from the center of the small circle to the axis of rotation is the radius of the great circle, which we will call \( R \).
   - The radius of the small circle is \( r \).

