\[
\cos A = \frac{AC}{AB} \implies AB = \frac{AC}{\cos A} = \frac{10}{\frac{3}{5}} = 10 \times \frac{5}{3} = \frac{50}{3} \approx 16.67 \text{ cm}
\]

Next, we use the Pythagorean theorem to find \(BC\):

\[
AB^2 = AC^2 + BC^2
\]

