   The formula for the length of an arc is:
   \[
   \text{Arc length} = \frac{\theta}{360^\circ} \times 2\pi r
   \]
   where \(\theta\) is the central angle in degrees and \(r\) is the radius.

   Given:
   \[
   \theta = 40^\circ, \quad r = 7 \text{ cm}
   \]

   Plugging in the values:
   \[
   \text{Arc length} = \frac{40^\circ}{360^\circ} \times 2\pi \times 7 \text{ cm}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Arc length} = \frac{1}{9} \times 14\pi \text{ cm}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Arc length} = \frac{14\pi}{9} \text{ cm}
   \]

2. **Calculate the perimeter of the sector:**
   The perimeter of the sector is the sum of the arc length and the two radii:
   \[
   \text{Perimeter} = \text{Arc length} + 2r
   \]
   \[
   \text{Perimeter} = \frac{14\pi}{9} + 2 \times 7 \text{ cm}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Perimeter} = \frac{14\pi}{9} + 14 \text{ cm}
   \]

3. **Convert the arc length to a decimal and add to the radii:**
   \[
   \frac{14\pi}{9} \approx \frac{14 \times 3.1416}{9} \approx \frac{43.9824}{9} \approx 4.8869 \text{ cm}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Perimeter} \approx 4.8869 + 14 \text{ cm} \approx 18.8869 \text{ cm}
   \]

