\text{Average steepness} = \frac{1}{20-0} \int_0^{20} f'(x) \, dx = \frac{1}{20} \int_0^{20} f'(x) \, dx
\]

By the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, we know that:

\[
\int_0^{20} f'(x) \, dx = f(20) - f(0)
\]

From the graph, we can see that \(f(0) = 0\) and \(f(20) = 32\). Therefore:

\[
\int_0^{20} f'(x) \, dx = 32 - 0 = 32
\]

Substituting this back into the formula for the average steepness, we get:

\[
\text{Average steepness} = \frac{1}{20} \times 32 = \frac{32}{20} = 1.6
\]

Thus, the average steepness of the climb over the interval \([0, 20]\) is \(\boxed{1.6}\).
