   \text{Area of the third rectangular face} = 10 \times 16 = 160 \text{ cm}^2
   \]
   The total area of the three rectangular faces is:
   \[
   192 + 160 + 160 = 512 \text{ cm}^2
   \]

3. **Calculate the total surface area of the triangular prism:**
