   \]

3. **Volume of the Composite Solid:**
   The volume of the composite solid is the volume of the rectangular prism minus the volume of the pyramid:
   \[
   V_{\text{composite}} = V_{\text{prism}} - V_{\text{pyramid}} = 1080 - 180 = 900 \text{ cubic cm}
   \]

Therefore, the volume of the composite solid is \(\boxed{900}\).
